ranslation and never an altar book. Its rubrics, its seasonal second and third orations, its Holy Week and its sanctoral are not those of 1962. It is carried only where a 1962 formulary is the same prayer, and nothing here may be used for recitation.\n\nThe 1861 keeps 29 November in its temporal, at the Vigil of St Andrew; leaf n530, printed p. 522, carries the commemoration's Collect, which this file already records, and leaf n531, printed p. 523, running head `29th NOVEMBER.`, carries `SECRET, of St. SATURNINUS.` with no Latin cue. It answers `Munera, Domine, tibi dicata sanctifica`. Page-image collation confirms that this historical English body answers the complete target Latin identity; publication is limited to the 1861 wording and does not claim that Cummiskey appoints the 1962 celebration.","lang":"en","rights":"public-domain","source_id":"edition.eugene-cummiskey.roman-missal-english-laity.philadelphia-1861","source_label":"The Roman Missal translated into the English language for the use of the laity, first revised edition (Philadelphia: Eugene Cummiskey, 1861)","text":"Sanctify, O Lord, the offerings we have consecrated to thee, and being appeased thereby, mercifully look down upon us, by the intercession of blessed Saturninus, thy Martyr. Thro'."}],"unavailable_translations":null,"untranslated":null},{"citations":[{"book":"John","loci":{"hebrew":[{"chapter":12,"first":26,"last":26}],"hebrew-unnumbered-titles":[{"chapter":12,"first":26,"last":26}],"vulgate":[{"chapter":12,"first":26,"last":26}]},"ref":"John 12:26","token":"John","unresolved":null}],"coverage":{"component":"scripture","cycle":"all","cycle_family":null,"languages":[{"availability":"unresolved","collation":"unresolved","lang":"la","publication_basis":"unresolved","relationship":"bible-reconstruction","witnesses":[]},{"availability":"unresolved","collation":"unresolved","lang":"en","publication_basis":"unresolved","relationship":"bible-reconstruction","witnesses":[]}],"occurrence_id":"roman-1